# oklch-studio needs no environment variables.
#
# The tool runs entirely in the browser. A seed color goes in, colorjs.io does
# the math, and every value on screen is derived on the client. There is no
# server, no API call and no credential to hold — so there is nothing to
# configure here, and nothing that could leak.
#
# This file exists to say that deliberately. A missing .env.example reads as an
# oversight and an empty one reads as unfinished; both send the next person
# hunting for configuration that was never there.
#
# If that ever changes, every variable gets listed here with a placeholder
# value and never a real one. One trap to know about first: Vite inlines any
# variable prefixed VITE_ into the client bundle, so that prefix makes a value
# world-readable by design. Public config may carry it; a secret never can.
